Changes to Oak's files (Apache 2.0, section 4(b)):

2026-10-02, the build spike:
- project.yml: DEVELOPMENT_TEAM set to the Pando owner's team; bundle ids and
  product name changed; FSShortName changed; the mach-lookup exception renamed.
- The extension's entitlements and DaemonClient.swift: the mach service renamed.
- OakMounterApp.swift: the extension bundle id renamed.

2026-10-02, mac-app lane (moved from spikes/oakfs to mac/):
- Files renamed: OakFS/project.yml to project.yml; HostApp/OakMounterApp.swift
  to HostApp/PandoApp.swift; Extension/OakFSItem.swift to
  Extension/PandoItem.swift; Extension/OakFSUnaryFileSystem.swift to
  Extension/PandoFileSystem.swift; Extension/OakFSVolume.swift to
  Extension/PandoVolume.swift; Extension/DaemonClient.swift to
  Extension/WireClient.swift; Extension/OakFS.entitlements to
  Extension/Extension.entitlements; OakFS/README.md to README.md (rewritten).
- Removed: Oak's logo (HostApp/Assets.xcassets/oak-dark.png) and Oak's app
  icon PNGs. The app icon and the window's lockup are rendered from the
  Pando mark (Icon/).
- project.yml: product "Pando" (Pando.app); bundle ids derived from one
  setting, PANDO_BUNDLE_PREFIX (ai.plannotator.pando, .extension, .broker);
  the extension's display name "Pando" and FSShortName "pando"; the broker's
  mach service ai.plannotator.pando.broker in the sandbox exception and the
  extension's Info.plist; profile names "Pando Developer ID" and
  "Pando Extension Developer ID"; version keys from MARKETING_VERSION.
- HostApp/PandoApp.swift: rewritten copy (the one switch, round 3 section 1b),
  Pando's Night palette, the Pando lockup in place of Oak's mark, and the
  extension bundle id read from the embedded .appex.
- Extension sources: types, log subsystems, volume and file system names
  renamed from Oak's to Pando's.

2026-10-02, mac-app lane, wire version 3 (docs/pando-fskit-wire-v3.md in
the ArtifactFS fork):
- Extension/Wire.swift: rewritten for version 3: internally tagged JSON
  headers with request ids, a raw payload for file bytes, 15 operations
  (setattr replaces truncate; symlink and forget added), paged readdir,
  the root as ino 2.
- Extension/WireClient.swift (was DaemonClient.swift): asynchronous XPC
  sends with request ids, a cap of 64 requests in flight, deadlines; the
  mount id instead of a socket path; the broker's mach service read from
  Info.plist.
- Extension/PandoVolume.swift: no FSKit callback blocks; reads and writes
  split at the daemon's limits; readdir passes cookies and the verifier
  through and pages; the item kind is remembered so removes need no
  getattr; createSymbolicLink and setAttributes (size, mode, times) added;
  consumedAttributes set; reclaimItem batches forget;
  supportsPersistentObjectIDs false; maximumFileSize; a nominal capacity.
- Extension/PandoItem.swift: linkCount 1, uid and gid, birthTime, rounded
  allocSize, parentID when known, integer time conversion.
- Extension/PandoFileSystem.swift: the hello handshake is asynchronous and
  checks for version 3; the volume name falls back to "Pando".
- New, not derived from Oak: Broker/ (pando-broker), Tests/, Icon/.
